envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-export-schema-database
type: schema
id: database
context: >-
  lib/node-schemas — shared canonical registry. Grounded in lib/node-index.js's real describe()
  output, which is itself derived from a real JaaStore instance's real tables.
intent: null
summary: null
system: null
tags: []
exported_at: 0
source: nexus.lib.node-export
payload:
  status: REAL
  source: >-
    lib/node-index.js's real describe() — every field below is read from a live JaaStore, not
    declared. §MCO17 2026-09-14 — James: "each database can be a .node also to connect to the
    associative lattice." §0.5/§16.7 were applied to this before building it, because a node
    describing a database is exactly the kind of abstraction that can be decoration: the test it
    had to pass was whether anything real consumes it. It does — intelligence/lattice/
    associative-lattice.js's updateEdge(from, to, ...) needs NAMED NODES to draw edges between,
    and by that module's own honest NOT BUILT YET footer, step 8 (event-triggered recompute) was
    unwired with "nothing calls updateEdge() yet" as of this build. A `.database` per system is
    the first real set of lattice endpoints this repo has produced. Without a consumer it would
    have been a decoration and would not have been built.
  fields:
    system:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: the real sovereign system that owns this database — its single write authority (§10.1, §17.1)
    dir:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: real on-disk directory of the JaaStore backing it
    tablePrefix:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: real JaaStore tablePrefix isolating this system's tables when a directory is shared
    tables:
      type: array
      required: true
      description: >-
        real list of {type, table, rows, firstSeenAt, lastSeenAt} — one entry per node type this
        system has actually written. A type with no writes does not appear: this describes what
        the system HAS done, never what it is permitted to do
    nodeTypes:
      type: array
      required: false
      description: real list of node type names indexed here — the same set as tables[].type, flattened for cheap filtering
    totalRows:
      type: number
      required: false
      description: real sum of rows across every table
    ts:
      type: number
      required: true
      description: real timestamp this description was taken — a description is a snapshot, never a live view
